course: dictionary
lesson: 2712
title: Dim: not bright, and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dim means not bright. A dim light gives only a little light. When you dim something, you make it less bright, like dimming the lights for a film.
explain: Dim can also mean hard to see. «Dive down and the light fades like evening: below about two hundred metres it is a dim blue twilight.» The sea is not bright there, so the light is hard to see clearly.
explain: Read the words around dim to find its meaning. «The dim light is red, because many night animals cannot see red well.» The words red and night animals show that dim means low light, not bright light.
explain: In everyday talk, dim can mean not clever, and this can be rude. Sentences such as «A bit dim» show this meaning, so use it carefully.
fact: Dim means not bright, so a dim light gives only a little light.
fact: To dim is to make or become less bright, as in dimming the lights for a film.
fact: Dim can also mean hard to see or remember.
fact: Dim can be used rudely to mean not clever, so be careful with it.
fact: Below about a thousand metres in the sea, sunlight is gone completely.
exercise: «A pet cat is a small hunter that lives on your sofa, and almost everything about its body is built for creeping up on prey in dim light.» What does dim light mean here? | Loud music | Bright red lights | *Not much light | Very bright sunshine
exercise: To dim is to... | Make a person very tall | *Make or become less bright | Make a loud noise | Make something wet
exercise: Your friend says you are «a bit dim» because you missed a joke. What does this mean, and is it kind? | It means you are hungry | It means you have a dim light on your bike | *It means not clever, and it is rude to say it | It means very bright and clever, so it is a compliment
test: «The dim light is red, because many night animals cannot see red well, so you can watch them without them feeling watched.» In this sentence, dim means | Very loud | Wet and cold | *Not bright, low light | Fast and quick
test: «Stare at your own face in dim light for a minute and it can seem to warp and change.» Which meaning fits best for dim? | Very tall and thin | *Not bright, so hard to see clearly | Very kind and friendly | Very hot and sunny
exam: Which word means the opposite of dim? | Soft | Heavy | Quiet | *Bright
